    {
      "id": "S2",
      "kind": "direct-local-source-fact",
      "fact": "Fixed-client GET authorization enters the reconciliation middleware, upserts the fixed client before provider auth.handler, closes the request Pool in finally, then awaits next. Reconciliation errors return 503 temporarily_unavailable. Additional authorize GET is not a pure metadata read because this existing flow writes the client record.",
      "refs": [
        "index.ts:2346-2408"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S3",
      "kind": "direct-local-source-fact",
      "fact": "GET /api/auth/oauth2/public-client requires sessionMiddleware and returns only client_id/name/uri/contacts/icon/tos/policy projection. It exposes neither secret nor resources/link. POST public-client-prelogin uses guarded prelogin middleware and the same projection; no claim that POST is a pure read or permissible for this task.",
      "refs": [
        "oauthClient/index.ts:425-465",
        "oauthClient/endpoints.ts:64-92"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S4",
      "kind": "direct-local-source-fact",
      "fact": "The provider resource API defines authenticated GET list/exact-resource reads, with SERVER_ONLY metadata and a session/resourcePrivileges gate. It returns a resource record and not its client links. In the inspected resource routes, linking exposes POST and DELETE only; no GET client-resource-link lookup exists. No assumption made about active runtime transport exposure beyond these source declarations.",
